sysml-rs local modifications to the SysML v2 standard model library.

Applied by tools/fetch-references/fetch.sh to the `sysml.library/` subtree of
the pilot implementation at commit 5a954377cd81e58f8ef8aba6222a2ce860d7787c,
AFTER the manifest's rename rules, so the paths below are the local layout.

Four files, two of them substantive:

  library.domain/Analysis/AnalysisTooling.sysml   cosmetic — trailing
      whitespace stripped on 10 lines.
  library.kernel/Collections.kerml                editorial — the Collection
      doc comment reworded and extended.
  library.domain/Geometry/ShapeItems.sysml        WORKAROUND — qualified
      redefinition targets (`Shell::edges::x`) reduced to bare `edges::x`
      because our resolver does not yet handle the qualified form. This masks
      an engine gap inside material presented as normative; it is an open
      conformance item, not a licensing one.
  library.systems/StandardViewDefinitions.sysml   NON-NORMATIVE ADDITION — 45
      lines defining UseCaseView, RequirementView and the bare-name view defs.
      SysML v2 does not define these; the added block says so itself.

The last two are tracked as conformance items (references-fetch-design.md §9
row 4). Do not silence this divergence by re-pinning the item's `sha256` —
`upstream_sha256` is what a pristine fetch produces, `sha256` is what a correct
local tree must have, and the gap between them is the disclosure.

